**filter(Predicate<T>) — keep elements where predicate returns true:**

```java
// Keep only settled trades
trades.stream().filter(Trade::isSettled)             // method ref
trades.stream().filter(t -> t.getAmount().compareTo(threshold) > 0)  // lambda
// Output: Stream<Trade> with fewer or equal elements
```

**map(Function<T,R>) — transform each element to a different type:**

```java
// Trade → BigDecimal (extract amount)
trades.stream().map(Trade::getAmount)                // Stream<BigDecimal>
// Trade → String (extract symbol)
trades.stream().map(Trade::getSymbol)                // Stream<String>
// String → Integer (string length)
Stream.of("RELIANCE","TCS").map(String::length)      // Stream<Integer>: 8, 3
```

**flatMap(Function<T, Stream<R>>) — one-to-many + flatten:**

```java
// Each account has multiple trades. Without flatMap:
accounts.stream().map(Account::getTrades)            // Stream<List<Trade>> — NESTED!

// With flatMap: flattens the nested structure
accounts.stream().flatMap(a -> a.getTrades().stream()) // Stream<Trade> — FLAT!

// Real example: each trade has multiple fees
trades.stream()
    .flatMap(t -> t.getFees().stream())              // Stream<Fee> — all fees from all trades
```

**sorted() / sorted(Comparator) — STATEFUL, buffers ALL elements:**

```java
// Natural order (Comparable):
Stream.of("TCS", "RELIANCE", "HDFC").sorted()       // HDFC, RELIANCE, TCS

// Custom Comparator:
trades.stream().sorted(Comparator.comparing(Trade::getAmount).reversed())  // desc by amount

// ⚠ STATEFUL: must pull ALL elements before emitting any!
// On infinite stream: Stream.generate(...).sorted() → hangs forever / OOM!
```

**distinct() — STATEFUL, uses internal HashSet:**

```java
Stream.of("RELIANCE", "TCS", "RELIANCE", "HDFC", "TCS")
    .distinct()    // keeps: RELIANCE, TCS, HDFC (first occurrence order preserved)
// Uses hashCode + equals internally → O(n) memory for seen elements
// ⚠ Objects MUST have proper hashCode/equals!
```

**limit(n) — short-circuiting, take first n:**

```java
trades.stream().filter(Trade::isSettled).limit(5)    // first 5 settled trades
// After 5 elements pass through → pipeline STOPS (short-circuit)
// Works on infinite streams: Stream.iterate(1, n -> n+1).limit(10)
```

**skip(n) — drop first n elements:**

```java
trades.stream().skip(10).limit(5)                    // pagination: skip 10, take 5
// Useful for manual pagination when DB pagination is not possible
```

**peek(Consumer) — debug observation, does NOT modify stream:**

```java
trades.stream()
    .filter(Trade::isSettled)
    .peek(t -> log.debug("After filter: {}", t.getTradeId()))  // debug ONLY
    .map(Trade::getAmount)
    .peek(amt -> log.debug("After map: {}", amt))              // debug ONLY
    .toList();
// ⚠ peek is for debugging ONLY. Do NOT use for business logic!
// In parallel streams, peek execution order is unpredictable.
// The JVM can SKIP peek calls if it determines they have no observable effect.
```

